{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788381802631,"sessionID":"ses_f9c24d349ffeKHnaVF2lrb6ncE","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_33d8483896bf49ecbc029578","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"Builtin::Sum\\|Sum =>\\|Float\" src/check | head -60"},"output":"grep: src/check: Is a directory\n","metadata":{"output":"grep: src/check: Is a directory\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"grep -n \"Builtin::Sum\\|Sum =>\\|Float\" src/check | head -60","time":{"start":1788381802627,"end":1788381802629}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Interesting! The JS backend's `Builtin::Sum` for anything not Int uses `tl_sum64` — i.e., for Float it uses `tl_sum64`, which starts `acc = 0n` (BigInt!), and then `BigInt.asIntN(64, acc + v[i])`. Wait, if v[i] is a Number (float), then `acc + v[i]` — BigInt + Number throws TypeError! That seems like a bug in the JS backend for Float sum... but wait, maybe the checker doesn't allow `sum` on a Vec of Float yet? Or maybe it does and the JS backend would crash. Let me check the tir checker for Sum builtin — what element types are allowed.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_063dcb071001MMbYcbbyFsTZS7","sessionID":"ses_f9c24d349ffeKHnaVF2lrb6ncE","messageID":"msg_063dca5cc001dXITFrlUEemae3"}}
